\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces Spatial distribution of the 397 charging stations across the Würzburg urban service area, with the central depot marked.\relax }}{3}{figure.caption.1}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces Two initial plan strategies for the same set of stations. Left: routing-efficiency approach visits A second despite low urgency. Right: maintenance-urgency approach defers A to last, ensuring critical stations are covered first.\relax }}{5}{figure.caption.2}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces Two replanning decisions under the same incoming disruption E. Left: dropping B (largest detour) leaves the most critical station unserviced. Right: dropping A (recently serviced, low power) allows B to be serviced and averts failure risk.\relax }}{7}{figure.caption.3}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4}{\ignorespaces Three-phase benchmark for the number of zones $k$. Top: Silhouette score. Middle: mean CFA total cost. Bottom: mean DB-Simple total cost. Each point represents the average over 100~simulation runs; colours indicate the benchmark phase.\relax }}{35}{figure.caption.4}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {5}{\ignorespaces Total cost distributions for all four policies under centrality-based zone selection (500 runs each). Boxes show interquartile range; whiskers extend to 1.5$\times $IQR.\relax }}{38}{figure.caption.6}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {6}{\ignorespaces Same-day rate versus total cost for all individual runs under centrality-based zone selection. Each point represents one Monte Carlo run; color indicates policy.\relax }}{39}{figure.caption.7}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {7}{\ignorespaces Total cost distributions for all four policies under centrality (light) and value-based (dark) zone selection (500 runs each). Boxes show interquartile range; whiskers extend to 1.5$\times $IQR.\relax }}{40}{figure.caption.9}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {8}{\ignorespaces Mean cost components (labor, travel, downtime) per policy and zone-selection mode. Bars with black border correspond to value-based selection. Dashed vertical lines separate policy groups.\relax }}{41}{figure.caption.10}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {9}{\ignorespaces Paired cost reduction (base minus rollout) per run for each policy. Positive values indicate the rollout lowered cost. Dashed line marks zero. All variants use value-based zone selection (500 runs each).\relax }}{44}{figure.caption.12}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {10}{\ignorespaces Distribution of replan overrides per run for all four rollout variants (500 runs each). Dashed vertical line shows the mean.\relax }}{44}{figure.caption.13}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {11}{\ignorespaces Cohen's $d$ for all key comparisons. Dashed vertical lines mark conventional thresholds (small: 0.20, medium: 0.50, large: 0.80). Zone-selection effects are the only comparisons with a large effect size; all other comparisons fall below the medium threshold ($d = 0.50$).\relax }}{48}{figure.caption.15}%
